  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[linkedin-for-pigeons]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[LinkedIn for Pigeons]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Thrilled to announce: I found a french fry.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Coo Endorsement
Open To Crumbs
Flock Network
Statue Review]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[A professional network for pigeons | Every pigeon on the town square, connected. 'Connected' means standing near each other.
Thought leadership for birds | Enable posts like 'What a dropped hot dog taught me about B2B sales'.
Pigeon recruiting suite | Headhunt top pigeons. The job is always 'stand on statue'. The pay is crumbs.
Carrier Pigeon Premium | Messaging, but an actual pigeon carries it. Delivery in 2 to 9 days, depending on wind.
Flock analytics | See who viewed your ledge. It was 40 pigeons. It is always 40 pigeons.
Expand to seagulls | A hostile market. They take what they want, especially down by the harbour.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Open to crumbs | As a pigeon, I want an 'Open to Crumbs' badge so that people with sandwiches can find me.
Humbled to announce | As a pigeon, I want to post 'humbled to announce' so that everyone hears about my new ledge.
Endorse for Head Bobbing | As a pigeon, I want to endorse my friend for 'Head Bobbing' so that he endorses me back.
Statue seniority | As a senior pigeon, I want my statue listed so that juniors know who sits on the horse's head.
Block the falconer | As a pigeon, I want to block the falconer so that he stops 'reaching out about an opportunity'.
Gap in my CV | As a pigeon, I want to explain my 2023 gap so that nobody asks about the chimney.
Meet a carrier pigeon | As a city pigeon, I want to network with carrier pigeons so that I can ask what a job is.
Daily engagement | As a PM, I want pigeons to post daily so that the graph goes up. They post 'coo'. It goes up.
Auto-congrats | As a busy pigeon, I want auto-replies that say 'Congrats!' so that I never have to read anything.
Hybrid roofing | As a hybrid pigeon, I want a different roof on Fridays so that I have work-life balance.
One crumb, 14 paragraphs | As a pigeon, I want to write a very long post about one crumb so that it can end with 'Agree?'
Client wants eagles | As a client, I want eagles on the platform so that it feels 'more premium'. Budget: pigeon.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Coo Endorsement | One tap to endorse. Skills: Pecking, Loitering, Strategic Flapping.
Flock Network | 1st, 2nd and 3rd degree connections. All of them are on the same roof.
Statue Review | Rate statues on comfort, view and head size. Employer reviews, but bronze.
Profile photo | Upload a headshot. Every photo is the same grey pigeon, slightly from the left.
Job title generator | 'Chief Crumb Officer', 'Senior Ledge Architect', 'Bench Evangelist'.
Who viewed your ledge | Premium only. Spoiler: it was a cat.
Skills assessment | A quiz: is this bread? Pass rate 100%, even when it is a cigarette butt.
Work anniversary | 'Celebrating 3 years on this lamppost.' 212 pigeons liked this.
Coo to text | Posts are transcribed automatically. Every post reads: 'Coo. Thoughts?'
Banner image | The default banner is a blurry bakery seen from above.
Hashtag suggestions | #OpenToCrumbs #FlockLife #GratefulForThisBench
Message by leg | Messages are tied to a foot. Character limit: whatever fits on a tiny scroll.
Follow a bakery | Get notified when the baker opens the back door. Our killer feature.
Pigeon of the Month | Chosen by algorithm. It is the round one from the high street. Again.
Out of office | 'I am currently on a roof with limited access to crumbs.'
Recommend a bench | Geo-tagged benches, ranked by crumbs per hour.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Pigeon endorsed itself 900 times | For 'Leadership'. We cannot prove it is a bug. It might be a strategy.
All users flew away during the demo | Someone clapped. Active users went from 300 to 0. They came back four minutes later.
Profile photo is a seagull | The user insists it is him. Facial recognition says 'bird'. Closing ticket.
Feed contains one post | 'Coo.' Posted 1.2 million times. Engagement is excellent.
Recruiter is a hawk | Three candidates accepted 'a quick coffee chat' and have since left the platform.
Notification hits the window | Push messages are delivered by flying into the glass. It works, but it is harsh.
Droppings parsed as signature | The CV parser accepts it. Technically binding in two municipalities. Legal is checking.
Five-star statue was a real man | He stood very still at a bus stop. Review removed. He was flattered.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[Messaging is literally pigeons | No queue, no retry. If the message gets eaten, it is eaten. 'Eventually consistent.'
User IDs are leg rings | Two pigeons share ring 0047. We treat them as one very active user.
Nest in the server rack | An actual nest. It has better uptime than the server.
Search only finds 'pigeon' | Every query returns all users. This has been 'good enough' for three years.
CooController.cs | 4,000 lines, one method: Coo(). Everything calls it. It also calls itself.
Built on a theme for dentists | Profiles still have a field called 'Dentist since'. The pigeons leave it blank.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[CEO Request: Get me verified | 'As a pigeon, if that is what it takes.' The blue tick is the goal. Cooing is on the table.
CEO Request: Go viral by Monday | 'Something with a pigeon in a suit.' No brief. No budget. One thumbs-up emoji.
CEO Request: Pigeons deliver the gifts | 'It is on brand.' 140 Christmas presents, one pigeon each. Facility has opened a window.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[I'm humbled to announce: a crumb.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[The professional network for pigeons. Grow your flock, get endorsed for Sitting on Statues, and share what a dropped hot dog taught you about leadership.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Grow your flock]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Thought leadership | Every pigeon has a hot take on bread. Now they have a platform. 'Agree?' is added automatically.
Endorsements that matter | Get endorsed for Loitering, Aggressive Walking and Stakeholder Management (Town Hall Square).
Open to crumbs | One green ring on your profile tells recruiters you are available. All pigeons are available.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[Coo. Thrilled to share that I have started a new position: this gutter.
I posted 'Hiring is broken' with a photo of a croissant. 40,000 reactions.
A recruiter reached out about an exciting statue. It was the same statue.
Endorsed for Navigation by 300 pigeons. I have never found the same place twice.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Free forever. Premium (4 crumbs a month) shows who viewed your profile. It was a seagull.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© LinkedIn for Pigeons. Views are my own and not those of my flock. We are all open to work.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
